\ Known five-stone results derived from section E of the canonical README.
\ The rows are checked independently against the arithmetic definition.
\ Native CAL v125 isolated=378 but appended the diagnostic despite success. This diagnostic is now conditional via a dedicated procedure.

To check the seed stones:
  Reach the stones for 1.
  If the current stones' wheat is not "17",
    put "The stone check failed at drop 1, wheat." into the check report; exit.
  If the current stones' barley is not "29",
    put "The stone check failed at drop 1, barley." into the check report; exit.
  If the current stones' salt is not "43",
    put "The stone check failed at drop 1, salt." into the check report; exit.
  If the current stones' bitter is not "71",
    put "The stone check failed at drop 1, bitter." into the check report; exit.
  If the current stones' red is not "101",
    put "The stone check failed at drop 1, red." into the check report; exit.

\ This procedure runs ONLY on mismatch. CAL's short If statement does not
\ guard a multi-line sequence, so the diagnostic has its own procedure.
To describe the second stone wheat mismatch:
  Put "The stone check failed at drop 2, wheat; observed=" into the check report.
  Append the current stones' wheat to the check report.
  Put "17" into the working stone formula's base.
  Put "29" into the working stone formula's neighbor.
  Put "2" into the working stone formula's extra.
  Put 3 into the working stone formula's factor.
  Calculate the working stone formula.
  Append "; isolated=" to the check report.
  Append the working stone formula's result to the check report.

